/P 169 0 R
/T (Literary Analysis is a demanding mental pursuit it involves annotation, reading and expert critical analysis. While close reading can untangle a head of Literature into an artichoke of themes, it provides far-flung assistance to balanced comparisons of hundreds or hundreds of thousands of works, performs, or archive containers of early editions in manuscript. Now, that it is posted and obtainable to the everyone through efforts like Venture Gutenberg \(PG\) and other repository sites, Digital Humanities has turned to pcs to define structures inside of Literature.)
/E (Literary Analysis is a demanding mental pursuit it involves annotation, reading and expert critical analysis. While close reading can untangle a head of Literature into an artichoke of themes, it provides far-flung assistance to balanced comparisons of hundreds or hundreds of thousands of works, performs, or archive containers of early editions in manuscript. Now, that it is posted and obtainable to the everyone through efforts like Venture Gutenberg \(PG\) and other repository sites, Digital Humanities has turned to pcs to define structures inside of Literature.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 169 0 R
/T (I think we began with the notion of our project Lit Mind as a concrete thing that takes what is merely raw novel text and turns it into a valuable knowledge. We talked about what type of a small project should definitely be considered valuable rather than just academically perfect. We felt that having to think about the difficulty of tracking characters and their relationships should be interesting but possible within the span of a semester.)
/E (I think we began with the notion of our project Lit Mind as a concrete thing that takes what is merely raw novel text and turns it into a valuable knowledge. We talked about what type of a small project should definitely be considered valuable rather than just academically perfect. We felt that having to think about the difficulty of tracking characters and their relationships should be interesting but possible within the span of a semester.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
