<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (However, while we were testing other tools, we came to the conclusion that almost all of them required users to annotate beforehand or they just worked really poorly on newsworthy literature with even a few paragraphs at all. There was not one easy-to-use, browserbased app that would take a version of the text from Dracula in the form of a Dracula.txt file and immediately identify the key players, their interactions with each other, and what all of these interactions meant. This is Lit Mind.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Another reason was the practicality of learning. Working on this project has given us insights into real NLP pipelines, API's and data visualisation which are all important skills for modern software developers. It was also an interesting chance to do some real-world graph theory, which we had only studied from a theoretical perspective in our algorithms class.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Lit Mind is a conjunction between latest Generation AI and conventional graph theory. It is an interactive, web-based platform for students, teachers, and literary researchers. The platform takes as input raw text \(.txt. Pdf\) files of plays and novels, and produces the data dashboards. Lit Mind automates six major analyses of the novel/play on the basis of:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Automatically extracting and de-duplicating entire character rosters from new text. Network centrality to mathematically distinguish primary lead characters from major supporting characters.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
