512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (The recommendations module employs an approach called content based filtering which is implemented by a Ridge regression model. To make recommendations, the user provides a csv file of books they have read with columns title, author, year, publisher, and optionally rating. The user must also provide a large catalogue of un-read books \(Books.csv\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Features from title, author, year and publisher are calculated with TF-IDF vectorizer. The model is trained to predict whether the user will like a book they haven't read based on the features and on similarities to the books they have read before. We do 5 fold cross validation to get an estimate of model performance \(AUC, R2 and MAE\). Recommendations are a.\) based on the catalogue books' scores b.\) from 20 top rated books and c.\) with feature level explainability of the prediction.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (4.6 Gemini Integration Module \(gemini_client.py\))
/E (4.6 Gemini Integration Module \(gemini_client.py\))
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (All communication with the Google Generative API is handled in this module. The module defaults to the gemini-3.5-flash model and falls back to a list of fallback models if the default is not available. A key design decision was to use the structured output mode where the API is instructed to respond with a JSON formatted response according to a predefined Pydantic schema, instead of freeform text. This makes the pipeline far more robust as there is no complex parsing of the output required.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (If the book was under 350,000 characters, I just sent the entire text to the API in a single call. If it's a longer book, I adopted the map-reduce strategy: I split the text into chunks of up to 60,000 characters, summarized each chunk in parallel in individual calls, and then summarized the summaries. This gets around the token limit errors AND gives you the big picture.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
