620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (At the most abstracted level, Lit Mind interact with two external domain: the User and the Google Gemini API. The User interact with Lit Mind through a request to analyze an uploaded novelty file and an optional API key that is used to fetch the analysis results. The Gemini API interact with the prompt as structured text and the response as structured JSON. { { { The core process of Lit Mind is to convert the raw text into the analysis outputs.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
621 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The four sub-processes for the highest level 1 lit Mind process are: Level 1 lit Mind process with sub-processes input Process 1.0 \(Text Ingestion\) input a file and output a text string \(textclean\). Process 2.0 \(Character Extraction\) input the text string and output a list of Character Result objects \(characterresults\). Process 3.0 \(Relationship Computation\) input the Character Result list and output the list of Relation objects with the relation name, the number of co-occurrences, and the range of Gemini classifications that can be a Gemini identifier \(cooccuringcounts\). Process 4.0 \(Visualization & Output\) input the list of Relation objects and output the Plotly figure, Pandas Data Frames for the tables, and markdown summary text \(viz_output\).)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The text buffer, just the clean text string \(held in memory\) The character registry, which is the Character Result dataclass \(The match metrics and text snippet\) held in the Streamlit session state The relation matrix, which is a list of Relation objects held in the session state)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
