732 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (APIqueries toGoogle GenerativeAI are completely authenticated \(authorization via environment variable GEMINIAPIKEY\). We use Gemini responsemimetype="application/json" configuration parameter and Pydantic schema validation to be sure that input requests always return deterministic \(parses without error\) schemas.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (API exceptions in a try/except block and display those to the Streamlit app for the user. This means that an API outage does not crash our app and our end user gets an informative error message.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (Google-generativeaiPython SDK\(0.8.3+\) used to interact with the Gemini API All API keys are stored as environment variables and are retrieved using python-dotenv - they are never committed into source code files or version control.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
735 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (Most challenging engineering problem was API request limit - For long novels \(which requires multiple API calls \(refer to map-reduce strategy to summarization\)\) - the tracker requests to the API multiple times in sequence, and the quota of the number of requests per minute is exceeded. This is tackled by the Gemini client module through retries with exponential backoff.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
