/T (The increase of 89% to 93.4% when using the Gemini API is caused by the alias review step, since Gemini can spot aliases which could not be detected by string matching \(e.g. The Count and Dracula would, to a human world knowledge reader, obviously be the same person but a string-matching algo can't do that\).)
/E (The increase of 89% to 93.4% when using the Gemini API is caused by the alias review step, since Gemini can spot aliases which could not be detected by string matching \(e.g. The Count and Dracula would, to a human world knowledge reader, obviously be the same person but a string-matching algo can't do that\).)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
932 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 191 0 R
/T (One failure, if you will, in the relationship type classification. For many pairs, the offline keyword-based classifier will label the pair as "UNKNOWN" because the keyword doesn't always appear in the same small window as the character names. The Gemini-based classifier does much better because it takes the context of the entire passage into account. This is the best scenario for using the API-based mode for relationship analysis.)
/E (One failure, if you will, in the relationship type classification. For many pairs, the offline keyword-based classifier will label the pair as "UNKNOWN" because the keyword doesn't always appear in the same small window as the character names. The Gemini-based classifier does much better because it takes the context of the entire passage into account. This is the best scenario for using the API-based mode for relationship analysis.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [25]
>>
